# llama-server profile for Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-UD-Q4_K_XL on this machine (E4, 2026-10-29).
# Measurements and rationale: bench/RESULTS-E4.md.
#
# Format: one flag per line (flag and value separated by a space, no quotes and no
# spaces inside the value), each with a comment right above it. Lines starting
# with # and blank lines are ignored.
# Left out, for the E5 wrapper to add: -m (MODELS_DIR), --host and --port
# (versions.env) and --api-key (secret kept out of git).
# Required environment variable: runtime/llama-server.env (GGML_OP_OFFLOAD_MIN_BATCH=1024).

# Model name exposed in the API (used by the agents in the "model" field).
-a qwen3.6-35b
# A single slot: there is one agent at a time; extra slots would split context and cache.
-np 1
# 131072-token context; the KV takes 1360 MiB in q8_0 (only 10 of the 40 layers have full attention).
-c 131072
# Flash attention: required for the quantized V cache.
-fa on
# K cache in q8_0 (q4_0 degrades tool calls).
-ctk q8_0
# V cache in q8_0, for the same reason.
-ctv q8_0
# All layers on the GPU (attention, DeltaNet, shared expert, output).
-ngl 99
# Routed experts of layers 0-37 in RAM and of the last 2 on the GPU (~1-2% per layer). Premise: dedicated GPU;
# ~470 MiB stay free (CUDA's view) and usage does not grow with context (measured up to 123k tokens).
-ncmoe 38
# --fit on only as a check: with explicit -ngl/-ncmoe it changes nothing; if less than the
# target is left, it just logs a "failed to fit params" warning and loads anyway (watched by the health script).
--fit on
# Minimum VRAM headroom for --fit (the 1024 MiB default is for a shared GPU; here it is dedicated).
--fit-target 384
# Logical batch of 4096 tokens.
-b 4096
# Micro-batch of 4096: each micro-batch pays ~0.9 s fixed (experts from RAM to GPU), so 4096 gives +45% prefill.
-ub 4096
# 8 threads for generation: 6-8 give the best result; 12 is ~3-5% lower and 16 drops ~25% (competes for WSL's 16 vCPUs).
-t 8
# 12 threads for the batches computed on the CPU (short turns under 1024 tokens).
-tb 12
# Load via DirectIO into pinned memory: +10-27% prefill vs mmap and load in ~30 s (none took ~2.5 min).
-lm dio
# The model's Jinja template, with the Qwen3 tool-call parser (already the default; explicit for clarity).
--jinja
# Keeps the reasoning of earlier turns: the resent history matches the cache token by token (f_keep = 1.0).
--reasoning-preserve
# Up to 48 context checkpoints per slot (63 MiB each, ~3 GiB of RAM at most).
-ctxcp 48
# Minimum spacing of 2048 tokens between checkpoints (default 8192). Kept from the plan; in the tests the checkpoints
# ended up at the end of each prompt and the effect of this value was not isolated (RESULTS-E4.md, question 9).
-cms 2048
# Prompt cache in RAM up to 12 GiB: keeps the main conversation when another comes in (subagent, title) and restores it.
--cache-ram 12288
# Prometheus metrics at /metrics (used by the validation runner).
--metrics
# Debugging (off in production): uncomment to log created/restored checkpoints and
# "forcing full prompt re-processing" (~10 KB of log per request, without the request contents).
#-lv 4
# Default sampling from the plan (section 7, model card); not measured in E4. The agent can override it per request.
--temp 0.6
# Same: top-p from the model card.
--top-p 0.95
# Same: top-k from the model card.
--top-k 20
